            'faq' => [
                ['Is LAF a clinic or hospital?', 'No. LAF does not run its own clinical services. Outreach is carried out with the District Health Offices and licensed health workers, and LAF provides logistics, mobilisation, counselling and community support.'],
                ['How do you work with government?', 'Through memoranda of understanding with both District Health Offices, joint planning of outreach days, a steering committee and reporting into the national system.'],
                ['Do you give medicines?', 'Government supplies are used first. The project buys only small amounts from licensed suppliers to fill gaps. LAF does not give antiseizure medicine; that stays with government treatment centres.'],
                ['Can lay counsellors treat trauma?', 'They offer brief, evidence-based support (WHO Problem Management Plus) under professional supervision. Severe cases are referred.'],
